#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0660-A expect=skipped domain=RS
#note "S1 (2026-09-14): RS without an RSCAT column. RSCAT is the ONLY thing that distinguishes the Clinical Classification use case from Disease Response, so without it the rule genuinely cannot decide -- Requirements.Variables.All [RSCAT] records one auditable skip instead of guessing. ⚑ RSEVALID is deliberately NOT gated: it is the rule's SUBJECT, and gating the leaf that makes a rule fire trades a finding for silence, which is what D-6's bound forbids."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#library codelist-terms CCCAT "CHILD-PUGH CLASSIFICATION" "H SCORE TOTAL SCORE" "PROTOCOL DEFINED RESPONSE CRITERIA"
dataset RS class=FINDINGS label="Disease Response and Clinical Classifications"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col RSTESTCD type=Char label="Short Name of Measurement"
col RSEVALID type=Char label="Evaluator"
---
S1 | RS | 001 | 1 | ADAS | INVESTIGATOR
